arket capitalization + USD debt - USD cash and short-term investments","dcf_model_ev":1157931.7,"ev_to_ebitda":2.5,"debt_to_ebitda":1.89,"net_debt_to_ebitda":1.52,"f_score":4,"f_score_breakdown":[{"id":1,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率 ROA > 0","passed":0,"detail":"當期 ROA = -7.9%"},{"id":2,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"營業現金流 CFO > 0","passed":1,"detail":"自由現金流 = $21,411M"},{"id":3,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率持續擴張 (ΔROA > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":1,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 63.2%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 1.04"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":472.9,"default_fair_val":472.9,"premium_pct":-96.9,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":24,"pe_forward":21.1,"pb_trailing":0.7,"pb_forward":0.6,"div_yield":7.33,"ps_ratio":0.4,"fcf_to_ev":24.53,"fcf_to_mcap":61.69,"liab_to_assets":63.2,"cash_to_assets":8.9,"current_ratio":1.04,"roe":-23.6,"roa":-7.9,"moat":{"ticker":"VOD","period":"2026Q4","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Vodafone 雖然是全球知名的電信品牌，但在電信產業中，品牌定價權相對有限。其服務本質上是基礎設施，價格易受競爭對手和監管壓力影響。雖然其品牌有一定號召力，尤其在歐洲市場，但與可口可樂或蘋果等消費品牌相比，其定價能力較弱。公司近年來面臨營收下滑和利潤壓力，顯示其品牌溢價轉化為定價權的能力不足。其品牌壁壘主要體現在客戶信任和服務穩定性上，而非顯著的價格差異化能力。","comment_en":"While Vodafone is a globally recognized telecom brand, its brand pricing power is relatively limited within the telecommunications industry. Its services are essentially infrastructure, and prices are easily influenced by competitors and regulatory pressures. Although its brand has some appeal, especially in European markets, its ability to command premium pricing is weaker compared to consumer brands like Coca-Cola or Apple. The company has faced revenue declines and profit pressures in recent years, indicating insufficient ability to translate brand equity into pricing power. Its brand barrier primarily lies in customer trust and service reliability, rather than significant price differentiation capability."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"電信業高度依賴特許經營權和監管牌照，Vodafone 在其營運的各個國家都持有重要的營運許可。這些牌照構成了一定的進入壁壘，尤其是在一些市場，新進入者難以獲得類似的頻譜和營運資格。然而，這些牌照並非專利，技術更新迭代快，且監管環境變化可能影響其權益。其壁壘主要來自於政府授予的營運權，而非技術創新帶來的專利保護，這使得其護城河具有一定的穩固性但非絕對。","comment_en":"The telecommunications industry relies heavily on operating licenses and regulatory permits. Vodafone holds crucial operating licenses in all the countries where it operates. These licenses form a certain barrier to entry, especially in some markets where it is difficult for new entrants to obtain similar spectrum and operating qualifications. However, these licenses are not patents, and technology evolves rapidly, with changes in the regulatory environment potentially affecting its rights. Its barrier stems mainly from government-granted operating rights rather than patent protection from technological innovation, giving its moat a degree of stability but not absolute."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"對於企業客戶而言，更換電信服務供應商涉及複雜的網絡整合、設備更換和服務遷移，轉換成本較高。對於個人用戶，雖然更換相對容易，但若涉及綁定合約、設備補貼或家庭套餐，也會增加用戶的轉換意願門檻。Vodafone 在企業通訊解決方案和物聯網連接方面，能有效鎖定客戶。然而，在競爭激烈的個人市場，用戶對價格敏感度高，轉換成本的約束力相對減弱，但整體而言仍構成一定的客戶黏性。","comment_en":"For enterprise clients, switching telecommunication service providers involves complex network integration, equipment replacement, and service migration, resulting in high switching costs. For individual users, while switching is relatively easier, it can still present a higher threshold if contracts, device subsidies, or family plans are involved. Vodafone can effectively lock in customers with its enterprise communication solutions and IoT connectivity. However, in the highly competitive consumer market, users are price-sensitive, and the constraint of switching costs is relatively weaker, though it still contributes to customer stickiness overall."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"電信網絡本身具有一定的網絡效應，用戶越多，網絡價值越高，尤其是在語音和數據傳輸方面。然而，Vodafone 的網絡效應相對有限，因為其主要服務是點對點的連接，而非平台型業務。雖然其龐大的用戶基礎和廣泛的網絡覆蓋能帶來規模優勢，但這更多是規模經濟而非典型的網絡效應。在許多市場，用戶可以選擇多家運營商，且服務同質化程度較高，這削弱了顯著的網絡效應。","comment_en":"Telecommunication networks inherently possess some network effects; the more users, the higher the network's value, particularly for voice and data transmission. However, Vodafone's network effects are relatively limited as its primary service is point-to-point connectivity, not a platform-based business. While its large user base and extensive network coverage offer economies of scale, this is more akin to economies of scale than typical network effects. In many markets, users can choose from multiple operators, and services are largely commoditized, which weakens significant network effects."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Vodafone 作為全球領先的電信運營商之一，擁有顯著的規模經濟優勢。其龐大的基礎設施投資、採購能力以及跨國營運經驗，使其在成本控制方面具備優勢。透過共享網絡資源、集中採購設備和優化營運流程，Vodafone 能夠降低單位服務成本。這種規模優勢使其在價格競爭中更具彈性，並能支持其在較低利潤率的市場中維持營運，是其重要的競爭壁壘。","comment_en":"As one of the world's leading telecommunication operators, Vodafone possesses significant economies of scale. Its substantial infrastructure investments, procurement capabilities, and cross-border operational experience give it an advantage in cost control. By sharing network resources, centralizing equipment procurement, and optimizing operational processes, Vodafone can reduce its cost per service. This scale advantage provides flexibility in price competition and enables it to maintain operations in lower-margin markets, serving as a crucial competitive barrier."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Vodafone 在歐洲和非洲部分地區擁有廣泛且深入的網絡覆蓋，這些地理資產是其核心競爭力之一。在這些地區，其網絡基礎設施的建設和維護成本高昂，形成了較高的進入壁壘。尤其是在一些新興市場，其先發優勢和對當地網絡的深度佈局，使其難以被競爭對手輕易複製。然而，其業務集中於特定區域，並未在全球範圍內形成獨特的地理壟斷。","comment_en":"Vodafone boasts extensive and deep network coverage in parts of Europe and Africa, which are among its core competitive strengths. The cost of building and maintaining network infrastructure in these regions is high, creating significant barriers to entry. Particularly in some emerging markets, its first-mover advantage and deep deployment of local networks make it difficult for competitors to replicate easily. However, its business is concentrated in specific regions and does not form a unique geographical monopoly on a global scale."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Vodafone 持續推動營運效率的提升，透過數位化轉型、自動化流程和網絡優化來降低營運成本。公司在整合收購的業務、精簡組織架構以及提升客戶服務效率方面取得了一定成效。儘管面臨行業挑戰，其在提升網絡利用率和降低維護成本方面的努力，使其能夠在競爭激烈的市場中保持一定的盈利能力。這種對營運效率的關注，是其維持競爭力的關鍵。","comment_en":"Vodafone continuously strives to improve operational efficiency by reducing operating costs through digital transformation, automated processes, and network optimization. The company has achieved some success in integrating acquired businesses, streamlining organizational structures, and enhancing customer service efficiency. Despite industry challenges, its efforts in improving network utilization and reducing maintenance costs enable it to maintain a certain level of profitability in a competitive market. This focus on operational efficiency is key to sustaining its competitiveness."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Vodafone 的資本配置策略面臨挑戰。公司過去進行了大規模的收購和基礎設施投資，但近年來營收和利潤增長乏力，股東回報受到影響。其資產負債表顯示較高的債務水平，限制了其進一步投資或回購股票的能力。雖然公司試圖透過剝離非核心資產和聚焦高增長業務來優化資本配置，但其過往的投資決策和目前的財務狀況，顯示其在資本配置方面的效率和決策能力有待加強。","comment_en":"Vodafone's capital allocation strategy faces challenges. The company has made significant acquisitions and infrastructure investments in the past, but revenue and profit growth have been sluggish in recent years, impacting shareholder returns. Its balance sheet shows a high level of debt, limiting its ability for further investment or share buybacks. While the company attempts to optimize capital allocation by divesting non-core assets and focusing on high-growth businesses, its past investment decisions and current financial situation indicate that its efficiency and decision-making in capital allocation need improvement."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Vodafone 在企業客戶市場透過提供整合的通訊解決方案和卓越的客戶服務，維持了較高的客戶留存率。對於個人用戶，雖然面臨激烈的價格競爭，但透過提供差異化的套餐、忠誠度計劃和穩定的網絡服務，仍能保有相當比例的客戶。其在物聯網和企業解決方案領域的佈局，有助於建立更深層次的客戶關係和更高的客戶黏性。然而，在高度競爭的電信市場，持續提升客戶留存仍是一大挑戰。","comment_en":"In the enterprise customer market, Vodafone maintains a relatively high customer retention rate by offering integrated communication solutions and excellent customer service. For individual users, despite intense price competition, it retains a considerable portion of customers through differentiated plans, loyalty programs, and stable network services. Its focus on the Internet of Things and enterprise solutions helps build deeper customer relationships and higher stickiness. However, in the highly competitive telecommunications market, continuously improving customer retention remains a significant challenge."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Vodafone 的業務具有一定的持久性，因為電信服務是現代社會不可或缺的基礎設施。其龐大的網絡資產和客戶基礎提供了穩定的收入來源。然而，電信行業面臨技術快速變革（如 5G、未來 6G）、激烈的市場競爭和嚴格的監管環境，這些都對業務的長期持久性構成挑戰。公司需要持續投入巨額資金進行網絡升級和技術創新，以應對顛覆性技術和新興競爭者的威脅，其持久性並非一成不變。","comment_en":"Vodafone's business possesses a degree of durability, as telecommunication services are essential infrastructure in modern society. Its vast network assets and customer base provide a stable revenue stream. However, the telecommunications industry faces rapid technological changes (such as 5G, future 6G), intense market competition, and strict regulatory environments, all of which pose challenges to the long-term durability of its business. The company needs to continuously invest heavily in network upgrades and technological innovation to counter threats from disruptive technologies and emerging competitors, meaning its durability is not static."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Vodafone 的經濟護城河呈現中等偏上的水準，主要由其龐大的規模經濟（M5）和在特定區域的地理網絡資產（M6）所支撐。其營運效率（M7）和企業客戶的轉換成本（M3）也提供了一定的保護。然而，品牌定價權（M1）和網絡效應（M4）相對較弱，且公司在資本配置（M8）方面面臨挑戰，影響了其整體護城河的強度與持久性。Vodafone 的業務模式更接近於基礎設施提供者，而非典型的收費橋或品牌型企業，其持久性（M10）雖有保障但易受技術變革影響。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Vodafone's economic moat is moderately strong, primarily supported by its significant economies of scale (M5) and geographical network assets (M6) in specific regions. Its operational efficiency (M7) and the switching costs for enterprise clients (M3) also offer some protection. However, its brand pricing power (M1) and network effects (M4) are relatively weaker, and the company faces challenges in capital allocation (M8), impacting the overall strength and durability of its moat. Vodafone's business model is closer to that of an infrastructure provider rather than a typical toll bridge or brand-centric company, and while its durability (M10) is somewhat assured, it is susceptible to technological changes.","evidenceHash":"828a012f665cda04599629cfaaa76cecacf050744f37b4fefb4a1d897c4e5f1e","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":"staleEvidence","evidenceHash":"828a012f665cda04599629cfaaa76cecacf050744f37b4fefb4a1d897c4e5f1e","currentEvidenceHash":"47f76a7f4b0ebcf1fd6f3b3fb76c9831e6d4c2ba8fdf5163f1376273833ba176"},"fScore":{"score":4,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-03-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"EUR","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-19T08:49:21.913Z","evidenceHash":"7863547b6e53fe444451c219b6bc06323268f92b78961e3cbec10e53711b16f3","mcapFx":{"asOf":"2026-11-18","from":"USD","to":"EUR","fromUsdPerUnit":1,"toUsdPerUnit":1.1154,"fromObservationDate":"2026-11-18","toObservationDate":"2026-11-06"}},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-03-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"EUR","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-19T08:49:21.913Z","evidenceHash":"7863547b6e53fe444451c219b6bc06323268f92b78961e3cbec10e53711b16f3"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/VOD.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/VOD.png","website":"https://www.vodafone.com","ceo":"Margherita Della Valle","full_time_employees":"91128","description":"Vodafone Group Public Limited Company provides telecommunication services in Germany, the United Kingdom, rest of Europe, Turkey, and South Africa. It offers mobile and fixed services; connectivity business solutions, such as digital services, the Internet of Things (IoT) and financial services; and IoT platforms. The company also provides cloud, multi-cloud, and edge computing solutions; M-PESA, an African mobile money platform to make payments and offer financial services; and international voice and roaming services. In addition, it offers unified communications, mobile connectivity, IoT connectivity, cloud and edge, E2E solutions, and security services; leases fibre and other fixed connectivity services; and engages in infrastructure assets, shared operations, growth platforms, retail, and service operations. The company serves private and public sector customers in health, banking and finance, transport and logistics, retail, utilities, and agriculture industries. Vodafone Group Public Limited Company was incorporated in 1984 and is based in Newbury, the United Kingdom.","description_en":"Vodafone Group Public Limited Company provides telecommunication services in Germany, the United Kingdom, rest of Europe, Turkey, and South Africa. It offers mobile and fixed services; connectivity business solutions, such as digital services, the Internet of Things (IoT) and financial services; and IoT platforms. The company also provides cloud, multi-cloud, and edge computing solutio